    {
      "description": "Admin-only. Update the APY bonus rate for a season. Two-phase gate: - Before `start_time`: any direction allowed (configuration fix). - `start_time <= now < vesting_end_time`: strictly increase only — decreases would punish users who already chose to wait based on the advertised APY. - `now >= vesting_end_time`: rejected — some users may have already claimed with the old value; the rate must stay consistent. New value is capped at `MAX_APY_BONUS_BPS` and any increase is rejected if the contract balance cannot cover the resulting worst-case payout (`max_outstanding`).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "update_apy_bonus"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "update_apy_bonus": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "airdrop_id",
            "apy_bonus_bps"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "airdrop_id": {
              "type": "integer",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            },
            "apy_bonus_bps": {
              "type": "integer",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    {
      "description": "Admin-only. Push `start_time`, `vesting_start_time`, and/or `vesting_end_time` forward before the airdrop begins. Each supplied field must be **strictly greater** than the currently stored value (forward-only — no shortening of the launch window or vesting). All existing invariants are re-checked against the resulting state: - `now < airdrop.start_time` (admin can only update pre-launch). - At least one field must be `Some`. - `new_start_time >= now` (no past). - `new_start_time <= new_vesting_start_time < new_vesting_end_time`. - `airdrop.expiry_time > new_vesting_end_time` (extend expiry first via `UpdateExpiry` if needed). Unsupplied fields fall back to the currently stored value.",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "update_times"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "update_times": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "airdrop_id"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "airdrop_id": {
              "type": "integer",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            },
            "start_time": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            },
            "vesting_end_time": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            },
            "vesting_start_time": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    {
      "description": "Admin-only. Extend `expiry_time` further into the future. The new value must be strictly greater than the currently stored expiry (forward-only — admin cannot bring the reclaim window forward and short-change unclaimed users). Permitted at any phase BEFORE the current expiry has passed: - `now < airdrop.expiry_time` (can't extend a passed expiry). - `expiry_time > airdrop.expiry_time` (forward-only). - `expiry_time > airdrop.vesting_end_time` (invariant preserved).",
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "update_expiry"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "update_expiry": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "airdrop_id",
            "expiry_time"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "airdrop_id": {
              "type": "integer",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            },
            "expiry_time": {
              "type": "integer",
              "format": "uint64",
              "minimum": 0.0
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  ],
  "definitions": {
    "Uint128": {
      "description": "A thin wrapper around u128 that is using strings for JSON encoding/decoding, such that the full u128 range can be used for clients that convert JSON numbers to floats, like JavaScript and jq.\n\n# Examples\n\nUse `from` to create instances of this and `u128` to get the value out:\n\n``` # use cosmwasm_std::Uint128; let a = Uint128::from(123u128); assert_eq!(a.u128(), 123);\n\nlet b = Uint128::from(42u64); assert_eq!(b.u128(), 42);\n\nlet c = Uint128::from(70u32); assert_eq!(c.u128(), 70); ```",
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
}
